WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:40.170
It had been four weeks since Anne
got hurt because of a dare.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:48.650
She couldn't go to school yet, and it was
difficult for her to leave the house.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:56.740
What are you doing?

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.600
Dinner's long been ready.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:03.000
Please, leave me alone for a while.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:07.110
What's wrong?
Is your ankle hurting again?

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:11.010
Diana didn't come to visit me again today.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.610
It's been four days now.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:20.780
Say, Marilla. Diana has always come to
visit me after school everyday.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.700
Do you think something has happened?

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.140
She must have had things to do.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.780
She will come tomorrow.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:33.170
What if... she doesn't like me anymore?

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:37.910
Anne, you shouldn't be
imagining things like that.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.770
Now come have dinner.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.570
Diana must have made a better
bosom friend than I.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.430
Please, I really have no appetite.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.310
Really!

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.540
Welcome back. Dinner's ready.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.220
Yes. I just met Mrs. Lynde.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:13.990
It seems Diana is...

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.490
What's wrong with Diana?

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.730
I know! I'll go see Diana now,

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:29.150
and ask her why she hasn't
come for four days.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:49.650
All right? You mustn't let Anne
know about this, Matthew.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.220
You're right.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:55.840
If she finds out Diana has
fallen ill in Charlottetown,

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.830
I don't know what she will do.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.960
Diana is ill?

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:11.410
Why did Diana go to Charlottetown?

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.510
She didn't even tell Anne.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:17.170
How should I know that?

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.840
What should we say to Anne if she asks?

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.500
Oh, Diana, If I had wings

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.540
I would soar to your side this very moment.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:09.320
The way I am now, there's no way I
could go to Charlottetown 30 miles away.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:13.800
Diana, why did you fall ill?

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:14.020
Please, don't do that, Marilla!

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:18.770
If you are worried about Diana,
why don't you ask Mr. Barry?

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:29.910
If she doesn't return from Charlottetown...

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:34.310
Please, Marilla, could you ask him for me?

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:37.160
Marilla, you'd better not go!

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.590
You'd better not go, Marilla!

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:41.140
My goodness!

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:45.990
I know you're worried about Diana,
but please do calm down.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:49.990
It shouldn't be a serious illness.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:55.480
If it was, Mrs. Barry would
be sure to inform you.

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:24.920
Dear Diana...

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.480
Do you remember the day we first met?

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:38.810
I solemnly swear to be faithful to
my bosom friend, Diana barry

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.290
as long as the sun and moon shall endure.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:16.070
I solemnly swear to be faithful to
my bosom friend, Anne Shirley

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.990
as long as the sun and moon shall endure.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:21.520
Do you remember the day we both vowed?

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:29.000
No matter how far the distance, I...
I'll always be by your side.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:38.580
I am your friend until death parts us.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:50.390
Diana,

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:55.320
I only had imagined friends in the past.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:03.350
I gave the one in the
mirror the name Katie Maurice.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:07.280
And when I lived in the mountains,

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:09.940
I imagined that the
echo was a girl called Violetta.

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:12.970
But...

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.720
Katie Maurice and Violetta,

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:19.240
were both friends of the past.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.170
Do you know why?

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:25.120
Because I've met you, my friend.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:34.530
Those happy days we spent
together will never come back.

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:37.250
Oh, Diana...

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:56.500
Please, Diana...

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:58.600
...get well soon!

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:07.730
Anne, the dinner is ready!
Come down quickly!

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:24.310
I was calling you just now,
at least have the courtesy to reply me!

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:31.450
What's wrong, Anne?

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.900
Really, that child.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:02.900
I really have to go ask Mrs. Barry about Diana.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:35.750
Mrs. Barry!

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:09.120
Anne, I'll leave the food here.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:11.210
Eat or the soup will become cold.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:15.510
With my mood now, I can't eat anything.

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:20.370
If you don't eat, you'll become ill as well.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.790
If it is for Diana...

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.850
I would bear any pain.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:33.950
Anne, I won't leave until you eat then.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:47.140
Now it's the season for peaches and pears.

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:53.570
Hear the cries of birds from afar,
the gathering of snow on mountaintops.

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:59.540
Life is slowly vanishing as
the mountain gather snow.

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:03.240
What a wonderful poem.
I feel so touched.

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:10.540
Life is slowly vanishing...

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:15.560
as the mountains gather snow.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:18.200
Anne!

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:24.250
Although there should be time for relaxation.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.710
Then let's see...

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:29.560
But... your spelling is disgraceful.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.790
Everybody look!

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:38.420
How could you sit in for lessons like this?

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:41.550
Don't mind that, Anne.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.750
The teacher is always like that.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:50.610
You've always been by my side
since I started school in Avonlea.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:44.660
Oh! You've always were
my most precious best friend.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:50.690
Carrots! Carrots!

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.400
You mean, hateful boy!

00:15:56.880 --> 00:15:58.290
How dare you!

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:05.800
Anne!

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:13.560
Anne, how could you?

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:16.870
I shall never forgive Gilbert Blythe!

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:22.280
You mustn't mind Gilbert
making fun of your hair.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.800
Why, he makes fun of all the girls.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:30.040
He laughs at mine because it's so black.

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:32.600
He's called me a crow a dozen times.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:33.150
No matter the case, you
were always trying to help me.
He's called me a crow a dozen times.

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:36.930
No matter the case, you
were always trying to help me.

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:43.770
And I've never done anything good for you.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:46.620
Should a boson friend be like this?

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:10.770
And Anne Shirley...

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:15.710
What's that horrible
thing in your hair? Take that off!

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:21.240
And since you seem to be so
fond of the boys company,

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:25.620
we shall indulge your taste for it this afternoon.

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:32.300
Now go and sit with Gilbert Blythe.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.980
What are you taking all those things home for?

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.580
I am not coming back to school any more!

00:17:56.950 --> 00:18:00.460
But, will Marilla let you stay home?

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:02.100
She'll have to.

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:04.330
I'll NEVER go to school again.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:06.990
You're mean, Anne! What shall I do?

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:11.320
Mr. Phillips will make me sit
with that horrid Gertie Pye.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:13.110
Do come back, Anne.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:16.290
I'd do almost anything in the world for you.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:21.190
I'd let myself be torn limb from limb
if it would do you any good.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.660
But I can't do this.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.140
Right...

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:32.820
I never once did any of your requests.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:39.060
When I think of it, my heart feels pierced.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:43.840
Diana, forgive me!

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:47.500
Please, forgive me!

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.130
And even after that,

00:18:56.510 --> 00:19:01.720
you visited me every day after school

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:05.750
to tell me about everything
that was happening there.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.300
The biggest thing that happened to us

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:14.500
was during the time I was absent from school.

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:20.930
It appears that something terribly
always happen when I am happy.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.990
That time I felt like I
was in the depths of despair...

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:32.900
Would there ever be a more cruel punishment
than not being able to communicate...

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:35.830
with your best friend next door?

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.120
Diana, what is the matter?

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:46.130
I'm... I'm awful sick.
I must go right home.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.860
That's enough!

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:19.260
It was Minnie May's Illness which
saved me from the depths of despair.

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:24.380
We never know when something bad
has good consequences.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:36.940
I never dreamt that my experience with
the 3 pair of twins would be of use here.

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:43.440
But besides saving Minnie May,
even your mother changed her opinion of me.

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:52.850
If your mother hadn't, my life would have
continued  to be in the black abyss of despair.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:21:00.880
Don't worry. The pressing need
for assistance has past.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:03.300
Minnie May...

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:05.530
Thank goodness, Minnie May!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:05.900
Thank goodness!

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:06.880
We stood together facing so many things.

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:08.000
Anne! Anne!

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:08.010
We stood together facing so many things.

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:09.000
Thank you, Anne!

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:13.420
Nothing in the world could ever
separate bosom friends like us.

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:29.090
How did you fall ill?

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:32.180
With my leg like this...

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:38.040
...how am I to go 30 miles to Charlottetown?

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.390
If I won't be able to see you ever again...

00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:01.800
Oh, Marilla, please leave me alone!

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.860
Let me cry all I want!

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:09.540
Oh, Diana!

00:22:09.940 --> 00:22:12.570
Why have you left me alone?

00:22:13.660 --> 00:22:14.930
Diana...

00:22:16.260 --> 00:22:18.050
What's wrong, Anne?

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:21.650
Diana!?

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:23.950
Aren't you sick?

00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:27.650
I just got back from Charlottetown.

00:22:30.780 --> 00:22:34.720
Aunt Josephine was ill,
so I went to visit her.

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:38.370
But her illness isn't serious.

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:49.480
Diana...

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:51.590
Diana!

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:57.460
I thought you wouldn't ever come back!

00:23:00.010 --> 00:23:03.020
I wouldn't be able to live anymore!

00:23:03.350 --> 00:23:04.560
Anne, really!

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:12.170
Anne, you can already
walk without anyone's help.

00:23:16.230 --> 00:23:17.280
You're right!

00:23:17.570 --> 00:23:19.060
I'm so glad, Anne!

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:21.200
Thank you, Diana.

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:52.720
Diana came back from Charlottetown just in time.

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:54.240
Right.

00:24:17.900 --> 00:24:20.040
In one day of Autumn,

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:24.250
Anne heard a wonderful plan
from Miss Stacy for Christmas.

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:27.570
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:27.740 --> 00:24:29.650
The Concert Plan

00:24:29.650 --> 00:24:30.630
Please watch!
